1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,428
Belle Gunness was a widow with a farm in

2
00:00:02,438 --> 00:00:03,586
LaPorte, Indiana.

3
00:00:03,816 --> 00:00:06,056
Many men who answered her ads were never

4
00:00:06,066 --> 00:00:06,678
seen again.

5
00:00:07,078 --> 00:00:09,703
She placed ads in marriage columns, many

6
00:00:09,713 --> 00:00:11,361
in Norwegian-language papers.

7
00:00:11,761 --> 00:00:13,698
One ad attributed to her sought a

8
00:00:13,708 --> 00:00:16,318
gentleman equally well provided, with a

9
00:00:16,328 --> 00:00:17,674
view of joining fortunes.

10
00:00:18,074 --> 00:00:20,473
Men came from across the Midwest, many

11
00:00:20,483 --> 00:00:21,346
with their savings.

12
00:00:21,746 --> 00:00:25,066
On April 28, 1908, the farmhouse burned.

13
00:00:25,296 --> 00:00:27,669
The three children in her care died, and a

14
00:00:27,679 --> 00:00:29,054
woman was found in the ruins.

15
00:00:29,284 --> 00:00:30,045
Was it Belle?

16
00:00:30,445 --> 00:00:32,061
Then searchers dug in the yard.

17
00:00:32,291 --> 00:00:34,304
At least a dozen people were buried there.

18
00:00:34,534 --> 00:00:36,556
Two were identified as men who had

19
00:00:36,566 --> 00:00:37,604
answered her ads.

20
00:00:37,834 --> 00:00:39,104
Most were never named.

21
00:00:39,504 --> 00:00:42,238
Her hired man, Ray Lamphere, was convicted

22
00:00:42,248 --> 00:00:43,229
of setting the fire.

23
00:00:43,459 --> 00:00:45,814
No one was ever convicted of the murders.

24
00:00:46,214 --> 00:00:48,217
For years, people said they'd seen her.

25
00:00:48,447 --> 00:00:51,279
A DNA test in 2008 couldn't settle it.

26
00:00:51,509 --> 00:00:53,510
LaPorte still doesn't know if Belle died

27
00:00:53,520 --> 00:00:54,281
in that fire.

28
00:00:54,681 --> 00:00:55,774
Did Belle get away?

29
00:00:56,004 --> 00:00:57,213
Tell us in the comments.

